/-
# The Cartan instance: the two sides of the cochain identity, in canonical form

For a `6`-simplex `τ` of a simplicial set `X` and a `2`-cocycle `x`, this file evaluates

* the seven summands `H(τ|k) = (cartanCochain X x)(τ|k)` of `δH(x)`, and
* the two summands `(x ⌣ x) ∪₂ (x ⌣ x)` and `(x ∪₁ x) ⌣ (x ∪₁ x)`

as explicit polynomials in the fifteen atoms `Fv X x τ 0 a b`.

The right-hand sides were computed with the python model `scratch/check2.py`; each identity is
proved by expanding the definitions (`genEval_cartanCochain`, `genEval_cup2`, `cup_apply_3_3`,
the face identifications of `CartanCompute`) and the twenty cocycle relations, and then closing
the resulting polynomial identity in `𝔽₂` (where `ring_nf` leaves coefficients to be reduced
modulo `2`).
-/
